<document xmlns="http://cnx.rice.edu/cnxml" xmlns:m="http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML">
   <title>2.3.5: Practice</title>
   <metadata xmlns:md="http://cnx.rice.edu/mdml">
      <md:content-id>m00413</md:content-id>
      <md:title>2.3.5: Practice</md:title>
      <md:uuid>6207154b-b57a-476c-ae69-38e85a079e24</md:uuid>
   </metadata>
   <content>
      <section class="practice" id="sect-00001">
         <para id="para-00001">Complete the following questions to practice the skills you have learned in this
            lesson.</para>

            <exercise id="d6f8070d-51ee-4e35-9188-c3c9a9779198" class="multiple-choice">
               <problem id="prob-00001">
                  <para id="para-00002">Lin is solving this system of equations:</para>
                  <para id="para-00003"><m:math><m:mrow><m:mrow><m:mo stretchy="true" fence="true" form="prefix">{</m:mo><m:mtable><m:mtr><m:mtd columnalign="left"><m:mn>6</m:mn><m:mi>x</m:mi><m:mo>−</m:mo><m:mn>5</m:mn><m:mi>y</m:mi><m:mo>=</m:mo><m:mn>34</m:mn></m:mtd></m:mtr><m:mtr><m:mtd columnalign="left"><m:mn>3</m:mn><m:mi>x</m:mi><m:mo>+</m:mo><m:mn>2</m:mn><m:mi>y</m:mi><m:mo>=</m:mo><m:mn>8</m:mn></m:mtd></m:mtr></m:mtable></m:mrow></m:mrow></m:math></para>
                  <para id="para-00004">She starts by rearranging the second equation to isolate the <m:math display="inline"><m:mrow><m:mi>y</m:mi></m:mrow></m:math> variable:
                     <m:math display="inline"><m:mrow><m:mi>y</m:mi><m:mo>=</m:mo><m:mn>4</m:mn><m:mo>−</m:mo><m:mn>1.5</m:mn><m:mi>x</m:mi></m:mrow></m:math>. She then substitutes the expression <m:math display="inline"><m:mrow><m:mn>4</m:mn><m:mo>−</m:mo><m:mn>1.5</m:mn><m:mi>x</m:mi></m:mrow></m:math> for <m:math display="inline"><m:mrow><m:mi>y</m:mi></m:mrow></m:math> in the first equation, as shown:</para>
                  <para id="para-00005"><m:math><m:mrow><m:mn>6</m:mn><m:mi>x</m:mi><m:mo>−</m:mo><m:mn>5</m:mn><m:mo stretchy="false">(</m:mo><m:mn>4</m:mn><m:mo>−</m:mo><m:mn>1.5</m:mn><m:mi>x</m:mi><m:mo stretchy="false">)</m:mo><m:mo>=</m:mo><m:mn>34</m:mn></m:mrow></m:math><m:math><m:mrow><m:mn>6</m:mn><m:mi>x</m:mi><m:mo>−</m:mo><m:mn>20</m:mn><m:mo>−</m:mo><m:mn>7.5</m:mn><m:mi>x</m:mi><m:mo>=</m:mo><m:mn>34</m:mn></m:mrow></m:math></para>
                  <para id="para-00006"><m:math display="inline"><m:mrow><m:mo>−</m:mo><m:mn>1.5</m:mn><m:mi>x</m:mi><m:mo>=</m:mo><m:mn>54</m:mn></m:mrow></m:math> <m:math display="inline"><m:mrow><m:mi>x</m:mi><m:mo>=</m:mo><m:mo>−</m:mo><m:mn>36</m:mn></m:mrow></m:math></para>

                  <para id="para-00007"><m:math><m:mrow><m:mi>y</m:mi><m:mo>=</m:mo><m:mn>4</m:mn><m:mo>−</m:mo><m:mn>1.5</m:mn><m:mi>x</m:mi></m:mrow></m:math></para>
                  <para id="para-00008"><m:math><m:mrow><m:mi>y</m:mi><m:mo>=</m:mo><m:mn>4</m:mn><m:mo>−</m:mo><m:mn>1.5</m:mn><m:mi>·</m:mi><m:mo stretchy="false">(</m:mo><m:mo>−</m:mo><m:mn>36</m:mn><m:mo stretchy="false">)</m:mo></m:mrow></m:math></para>
                  <para id="para-00009"><m:math><m:mrow><m:mi>y</m:mi><m:mo>=</m:mo><m:mn>58</m:mn></m:mrow></m:math></para>
                  <para id="para-00010">Does Lin’s solution of <m:math display="inline"><m:mrow><m:mo stretchy="false">(</m:mo><m:mo>−</m:mo><m:mn>36</m:mn><m:mo>,</m:mo><m:mn>58</m:mn><m:mo stretchy="false">)</m:mo></m:mrow></m:math> makes both equations in the system
                     true?</para>
                  <para id="para-00011">Multiple Choice:</para>
                  <para id="para-00012">yes; Her solution makes both equations true.</para>
                  <para id="para-00013">No; Her solution does not make both equations true.</para>
               </problem>
               <solution id="sol-00001">
                  <para id="para-00014">Correct! No; Her solution does not make both equations true.</para>
                  <para id="para-00015">Try again. Revisit activity 2.3.2.</para>
                  <para id="para-00016">The correct answer is that Lin’s solution does not make both equations true.</para>
               </solution>
            </exercise>

            <exercise id="fc2e0fa3-9cd1-4dff-987c-17aa1afa8afd" class="multiple-choice">
               <problem id="prob-00002">
                  <para id="para-00017">Which of the following is true of Lin’s solution?</para>
                  <para id="para-00018">Multiple Choice:</para>
                  <para id="para-00019">Lin made a multiplication error. The correct answer is <m:math display="inline"><m:mrow><m:mi>x</m:mi><m:mo>=</m:mo><m:mn>4</m:mn></m:mrow></m:math> and \(y =
                     -2\), or <m:math display="inline"><m:mrow><m:mo stretchy="false">(</m:mo><m:mn>4</m:mn><m:mo>,</m:mo><m:mo>−</m:mo><m:mn>2</m:mn><m:mo stretchy="false">)</m:mo><m:mo>.</m:mo></m:mrow></m:math></para>
                  <para id="para-00020">Lin made a multiplication error. The correct answer is <m:math display="inline"><m:mrow><m:mi>x</m:mi><m:mo>=</m:mo><m:mn>9</m:mn></m:mrow></m:math> and \(y =
                     4\), or (9,4).</para>
                  <para id="para-00021">Lin made an addition error. The correct answer is <m:math display="inline"><m:mrow><m:mi>x</m:mi><m:mo>=</m:mo><m:mn>0</m:mn></m:mrow></m:math> and <m:math display="inline"><m:mrow><m:mi>y</m:mi><m:mo>=</m:mo><m:mn>4</m:mn></m:mrow></m:math>,
                     or (0,4).</para>
                  <para id="para-00022">Lin’s solution of (-36, 58) is correct.</para>
               </problem>
               <solution id="sol-00002">
                  <para id="para-00023">Correct! Lin made a multiplication error. The correct answer is x = 4 and y
                     = -2, or (4,-2).</para>
                  <para id="para-00024">Try again. Revisit activity 2.3.2.</para>
                  <para id="para-00025">The correct answer is Lin made a multiplication error. The correct answer is
                     <m:math display="inline"><m:mrow><m:mi>x</m:mi><m:mo>=</m:mo><m:mn>4</m:mn></m:mrow></m:math> and <m:math display="inline"><m:mrow><m:mi>y</m:mi><m:mo>=</m:mo><m:mo>−</m:mo><m:mn>2</m:mn></m:mrow></m:math>, or <m:math display="inline"><m:mrow><m:mo stretchy="false">(</m:mo><m:mn>4</m:mn><m:mo>,</m:mo><m:mo>−</m:mo><m:mn>2</m:mn><m:mo stretchy="false">)</m:mo></m:mrow></m:math>.</para>
               </solution>
            </exercise>

         <para id="para-00026">In 3 - 9, solve the systems of equations by substitution.</para>
            <exercise id="a42eaa70-a2fc-4597-8102-6b37c1b48ad6" class="multiple-choice">
               <problem id="prob-00003">
                  <para id="para-00027"><m:math><m:mrow><m:mrow><m:mo stretchy="true" fence="true" form="prefix">{</m:mo><m:mtable><m:mtr><m:mtd columnalign="left"><m:mn>2</m:mn><m:mi>x</m:mi><m:mo>+</m:mo><m:mi>y</m:mi><m:mo>=</m:mo><m:mo>−</m:mo><m:mn>2</m:mn></m:mtd></m:mtr><m:mtr><m:mtd columnalign="left"><m:mn>3</m:mn><m:mi>x</m:mi><m:mo>−</m:mo><m:mi>y</m:mi><m:mo>=</m:mo><m:mn>7</m:mn></m:mtd></m:mtr></m:mtable><m:mo stretchy="true" fence="true" form="postfix"/></m:mrow></m:mrow></m:math></para>
                  <para id="para-00028">Multiple Choice:</para>
                  <para id="para-00029"><m:math><m:mrow><m:mo stretchy="false">(</m:mo><m:mi>−</m:mi><m:mn>1</m:mn><m:mo>,</m:mo><m:mn>0</m:mn><m:mo stretchy="false">)</m:mo></m:mrow></m:math></para>
                  <para id="para-00030"><m:math><m:mrow><m:mo stretchy="false">(</m:mo><m:mn>0</m:mn><m:mo>,</m:mo><m:mi>−</m:mi><m:mn>2</m:mn><m:mo stretchy="false">)</m:mo></m:mrow></m:math></para>
                  <para id="para-00031"><m:math><m:mrow><m:mo stretchy="false">(</m:mo><m:mn>1</m:mn><m:mo>,</m:mo><m:mi>−</m:mi><m:mn>4</m:mn><m:mo stretchy="false">)</m:mo></m:mrow></m:math></para>
                  <para id="para-00032"><m:math><m:mrow><m:mo stretchy="false">(</m:mo><m:mn>2</m:mn><m:mo>,</m:mo><m:mn>6</m:mn><m:mo stretchy="false">)</m:mo></m:mrow></m:math></para>
               </problem>
               <solution id="sol-00003">
                  <para id="para-00033">Correct! (1,−4)</para>
                  <para id="para-00034">Try again. Revisit activities 2.3.3 and 2.3.4.</para>
                  <para id="para-00035">The correct answer is <m:math display="inline"><m:mrow><m:mo stretchy="false">(</m:mo><m:mn>1</m:mn><m:mo>,</m:mo><m:mi>−</m:mi><m:mn>4</m:mn><m:mo stretchy="false">)</m:mo></m:mrow></m:math>.</para>
                  <para id="para-00036">Check the solution in both equations.</para>
                  <para id="para-00037">\(\begin{array}{rcl}2x+y&amp;=&amp;-2 \\ 2(1)+(-4)&amp;=&amp;-2 \\
                     2-4&amp;=&amp;-2 \\ -2&amp;=&amp;-2\checkmark \\ \end{array}\)</para>
                  <para id="para-00038">\(\begin{array}{rcl}3x-y&amp;=&amp;7 \\ 3(1)-(-4)&amp;=&amp;7 \\
                     3+4&amp;=&amp;7 \\ 7&amp;=&amp;7\checkmark \\ \end{array}\)</para>
                  <para id="para-00039">(4,-1) Makes both equations in the system true, therefore it is a solution.</para>
               </solution>
            </exercise>

            <exercise id="_527afbcf-da67-43bf-a980-73f4d3ab4824" class="multiple-choice">
               <problem id="prob-00004">
                  <para id="para-00040"><m:math><m:mrow><m:mrow><m:mo stretchy="true" fence="true" form="prefix">{</m:mo><m:mtable><m:mtr><m:mtd columnalign="left"><m:mi>x</m:mi><m:mo>−</m:mo><m:mn>3</m:mn><m:mi>y</m:mi><m:mo>=</m:mo><m:mo>−</m:mo><m:mn>9</m:mn></m:mtd></m:mtr><m:mtr><m:mtd columnalign="left"><m:mn>2</m:mn><m:mi>x</m:mi><m:mo>+</m:mo><m:mn>5</m:mn><m:mi>y</m:mi><m:mo>=</m:mo><m:mn>4</m:mn></m:mtd></m:mtr></m:mtable><m:mo stretchy="true" fence="true" form="postfix"/></m:mrow></m:mrow></m:math></para>
                  <para id="para-00041">Multiple Choice:</para>
                  <para id="para-00042"><m:math><m:mrow><m:mo stretchy="false">(</m:mo><m:mi>−</m:mi><m:mn>6</m:mn><m:mo>,</m:mo><m:mn>1</m:mn><m:mo stretchy="false">)</m:mo></m:mrow></m:math></para>
                  <para id="para-00043"><m:math><m:mrow><m:mo stretchy="false">(</m:mo><m:mn>2</m:mn><m:mo>,</m:mo><m:mn>0</m:mn><m:mo stretchy="false">)</m:mo></m:mrow></m:math></para>
                  <para id="para-00044"><m:math><m:mrow><m:mo stretchy="false">(</m:mo><m:mn>0</m:mn><m:mo>,</m:mo><m:mn>3</m:mn><m:mo stretchy="false">)</m:mo></m:mrow></m:math></para>
                  <para id="para-00045"><m:math><m:mrow><m:mo stretchy="false">(</m:mo><m:mi>−</m:mi><m:mn>3</m:mn><m:mo>,</m:mo><m:mn>2</m:mn><m:mo stretchy="false">)</m:mo></m:mrow></m:math></para>
               </problem>
               <solution id="sol-00004">
                  <para id="para-00046">Correct! (−3,2)</para>
                  <para id="para-00047">Try again. Revisit activities 2.3.3 and 2.3.4.</para>
                  <para id="para-00048">The correct answer is (−3,2).</para>
                  <para id="para-00049">Check the solution in both equations.</para>
                  <para id="para-00050">\(\begin{array}{rcl}x−3y&amp;=&amp;−9 \\ (-3)−3(2)&amp;=&amp;−9 \\
                     -3−6=&amp;−&amp;9 \\ -9&amp;=&amp;-9\checkmark \\ \end{array}\)</para>
                  <para id="para-00051">\(\begin{array}{rcl}2x+5y=4 \\ 2(-3)+5(2)&amp;=&amp;4 \\ -6+10&amp;=&amp;4
                     \\ 4&amp;=&amp;4\checkmark \\ \end{array}\)</para>
                  <para id="para-00052">(-3,2) Makes both equations in the system true, therefore it is a solution.</para>
               </solution>
            </exercise>
            <exercise id="_6193e47f-ea4f-4dce-ad7b-26c2028856de" class="multiple-choice">
               <problem id="prob-00005">
                  <para id="para-00053"><m:math><m:mrow><m:mrow><m:mo stretchy="true" fence="true" form="prefix">{</m:mo><m:mtable><m:mtr><m:mtd columnalign="left"><m:mo>−</m:mo><m:mn>2</m:mn><m:mi>x</m:mi><m:mo>+</m:mo><m:mn>2</m:mn><m:mi>y</m:mi><m:mo>=</m:mo><m:mn>6</m:mn></m:mtd></m:mtr><m:mtr><m:mtd columnalign="left"><m:mn>2</m:mn><m:mi>y</m:mi><m:mo>=</m:mo><m:mo>−</m:mo><m:mn>6</m:mn><m:mi>x</m:mi><m:mo>+</m:mo><m:mn>14</m:mn></m:mtd></m:mtr></m:mtable><m:mo stretchy="true" fence="true" form="postfix"/></m:mrow></m:mrow></m:math></para>
                  <para id="para-00054">Multiple Choice:</para>
                  <para id="para-00055"><m:math><m:mrow><m:mo stretchy="false">(</m:mo><m:mn>1</m:mn><m:mo>,</m:mo><m:mn>4</m:mn><m:mo stretchy="false">)</m:mo></m:mrow></m:math></para>
                  <para id="para-00056"><m:math><m:mrow><m:mo stretchy="false">(</m:mo><m:mn>0</m:mn><m:mo>,</m:mo><m:mn>7</m:mn><m:mo stretchy="false">)</m:mo></m:mrow></m:math></para>
                  <para id="para-00057"><m:math><m:mrow><m:mo stretchy="false">(</m:mo><m:mn>2</m:mn><m:mo>,</m:mo><m:mn>1</m:mn><m:mo stretchy="false">)</m:mo></m:mrow></m:math></para>
                  <para id="para-00058"><m:math><m:mrow><m:mo stretchy="false">(</m:mo><m:mi>−</m:mi><m:mn>3</m:mn><m:mo>,</m:mo><m:mn>0</m:mn><m:mo stretchy="false">)</m:mo></m:mrow></m:math></para>
               </problem>
               <solution id="sol-00005">
                  <para id="para-00059">Correct! (1,4)</para>
                  <para id="para-00060">Try again. Revisit activities 2.3.3 and 2.3.4.</para>
                  <para id="para-00061">The correct answer is (1,4).</para>
                  <para id="para-00062">\(\begin{array}{rcl}−2x+2y&amp;=&amp;6 \\ −2(1)+2(4)&amp;=&amp;6 \\
                     −2+8&amp;=&amp;6 \\ 6&amp;=&amp;6\checkmark \\ \end{array}\)</para>
                  <para id="para-00063">\(\begin{array}{rcl}2y&amp;=&amp;−6x+14 \\ 2(4)&amp;=&amp;−6(1)+14 \\
                     8&amp;=&amp;−6+14 \\ 8&amp;=&amp;8\checkmark \\ \end{array}\)</para>
                  <para id="para-00064">(1,4) Makes both equations in the system true, therefore it is a solution.</para>
               </solution>
            </exercise>
            <exercise id="_96fbcd3b-ef40-4cf3-b0a4-0f88ccb60448" class="multiple-choice">
               <problem id="prob-00006">
                  <para id="para-00065"><m:math><m:mrow><m:mrow><m:mo stretchy="true" fence="true" form="prefix">{</m:mo><m:mtable><m:mtr><m:mtd columnalign="left"><m:mn>3</m:mn><m:mi>x</m:mi><m:mo>+</m:mo><m:mn>4</m:mn><m:mi>y</m:mi><m:mo>=</m:mo><m:mn>1</m:mn></m:mtd></m:mtr><m:mtr><m:mtd columnalign="left"><m:mi>y</m:mi><m:mo>=</m:mo><m:mo>−</m:mo><m:mfrac><m:mn>2</m:mn><m:mn>5</m:mn></m:mfrac><m:mi>x</m:mi><m:mo>+</m:mo><m:mn>2</m:mn></m:mtd></m:mtr></m:mtable><m:mo stretchy="true" fence="true" form="postfix"/></m:mrow></m:mrow></m:math></para>
                  <para id="para-00066">Multiple Choice:</para>
                  <para id="para-00067"><m:math><m:mrow><m:mo stretchy="false">(</m:mo><m:mn>5</m:mn><m:mo>,</m:mo><m:mn>0</m:mn><m:mo stretchy="false">)</m:mo></m:mrow></m:math></para>
                  <para id="para-00068"><m:math><m:mrow><m:mo stretchy="false">(</m:mo><m:mn>0</m:mn><m:mo>,</m:mo><m:mn>2</m:mn><m:mo stretchy="false">)</m:mo></m:mrow></m:math></para>
                  <para id="para-00069"><m:math><m:mrow><m:mo stretchy="false">(</m:mo><m:mi>−</m:mi><m:mn>1</m:mn><m:mo>,</m:mo><m:mn>1</m:mn><m:mo stretchy="false">)</m:mo></m:mrow></m:math></para>
                  <para id="para-00070"><m:math><m:mrow><m:mo stretchy="false">(</m:mo><m:mi>−</m:mi><m:mn>5</m:mn><m:mo>,</m:mo><m:mn>4</m:mn><m:mo stretchy="false">)</m:mo></m:mrow></m:math></para>
               </problem>
               <solution id="sol-00006">
                  <para id="para-00071">Correct! (−5,4)</para>
                  <para id="para-00072">Try again. Revisit activities 2.3.3 and 2.3.4.</para>
                  <para id="para-00073">The correct answer is (−5,4).</para>
                  <para id="para-00074">Check the solution in both equations.</para>
                  <para id="para-00075">\(\begin{array}{rcl} 3x+4y&amp;=&amp;1 \\ 3(-5)+4(4)&amp;=&amp;1 \\
                     −15+16&amp;=&amp;1 \\ 6&amp;=&amp;6\checkmark \\ \end{array}\)</para>
                  <para id="para-00076">\(\begin{array}{rcl} y&amp;=&amp;−25x+2 \\ 4&amp;=&amp;−25(-5)+2 \\
                     4&amp;=&amp;2+2 \\ 4&amp;=&amp;4\checkmark \\ \end{array}\)</para>
                  <para id="para-00077">(−5,4) Makes both equations in the system true, therefore it is a solution.</para>
               </solution>
            </exercise>
            <exercise id="ade4892d-a5f1-4d15-b82a-1e79e6d4d8c9" class="multiple-choice">
               <problem id="prob-00007">
                  <para id="para-00078"><m:math><m:mrow><m:mrow><m:mo stretchy="true" fence="true" form="prefix">{</m:mo><m:mtable><m:mtr><m:mtd columnalign="left"><m:mn>3</m:mn><m:mi>x</m:mi><m:mo>+</m:mo><m:mi>y</m:mi><m:mo>=</m:mo><m:mn>10</m:mn></m:mtd></m:mtr><m:mtr><m:mtd columnalign="left"><m:mi>x</m:mi><m:mo>−</m:mo><m:mn>2</m:mn><m:mi>y</m:mi><m:mo>=</m:mo><m:mo>−</m:mo><m:mn>20</m:mn></m:mtd></m:mtr></m:mtable><m:mo stretchy="true" fence="true" form="postfix"/></m:mrow></m:mrow></m:math></para>
                  <para id="para-00079">Multiple Choice:</para>
                  <para id="para-00080"><m:math><m:mrow><m:mo stretchy="false">(</m:mo><m:mn>2</m:mn><m:mo>,</m:mo><m:mn>2</m:mn><m:mo stretchy="false">)</m:mo></m:mrow></m:math></para>
                  <para id="para-00081"><m:math><m:mrow><m:mo stretchy="false">(</m:mo><m:mn>0</m:mn><m:mo>,</m:mo><m:mn>10</m:mn><m:mo stretchy="false">)</m:mo></m:mrow></m:math></para>
                  <para id="para-00082"><m:math><m:mrow><m:mo stretchy="false">(</m:mo><m:mi>−</m:mi><m:mn>4</m:mn><m:mo>,</m:mo><m:mn>8</m:mn><m:mo stretchy="false">)</m:mo></m:mrow></m:math></para>
                  <para id="para-00083"><m:math><m:mrow><m:mo stretchy="false">(</m:mo><m:mn>4</m:mn><m:mo>,</m:mo><m:mn>12</m:mn><m:mo stretchy="false">)</m:mo></m:mrow></m:math></para>
               </problem>
               <solution id="sol-00007">
                  <para id="para-00084">Correct! (0,10)</para>
                  <para id="para-00085">Try again. Revisit activities 2.3.3 and 2.3.4.</para>
                  <para id="para-00086">The correct answer is (0,10).</para>
                  <para id="para-00087">Check the solution in both equations.</para>
                  <para id="para-00088">\(\begin{array}{rcl}4x+y&amp;=&amp;10 \\ 4(0)+(10)&amp;=&amp;10 \\
                     0+10&amp;=&amp;10 \\ 10&amp;=&amp;10\checkmark \\ \end{array}\)</para>
                  <para id="para-00089">\(\begin{array}{rcl}x−2y&amp;=&amp;−20 \\ 0−2(10)&amp;=&amp;−20 \\
                     0−20&amp;=&amp;−20 \\ -20&amp;=&amp;-20\checkmark \\ \end{array}\)</para>
                  <para id="para-00090">(0,10) Makes both equations in the system true, therefore it is a solution.</para>
               </solution>
            </exercise>
            <exercise id="_59b0d4f7-31f5-453a-b7e2-1c74c33f9fda" class="multiple-choice">
               <problem id="prob-00008">
                  <para id="para-00091"><m:math><m:mrow><m:mrow><m:mo stretchy="true" fence="true" form="prefix">{</m:mo><m:mtable><m:mtr><m:mtd columnalign="left"><m:mi>y</m:mi><m:mo>=</m:mo><m:mi>x</m:mi><m:mo>−</m:mo><m:mn>6</m:mn></m:mtd></m:mtr><m:mtr><m:mtd columnalign="left"><m:mi>y</m:mi><m:mo>=</m:mo><m:mo>−</m:mo><m:mfrac><m:mn>3</m:mn><m:mn>2</m:mn></m:mfrac><m:mi>x</m:mi><m:mo>+</m:mo><m:mn>4</m:mn></m:mtd></m:mtr></m:mtable><m:mo stretchy="true" fence="true" form="postfix"/></m:mrow></m:mrow></m:math></para>
                  <para id="para-00092">Multiple Choice:</para>
                  <para id="para-00093"><m:math><m:mrow><m:mo stretchy="false">(</m:mo><m:mn>6</m:mn><m:mo>,</m:mo><m:mn>0</m:mn><m:mo stretchy="false">)</m:mo></m:mrow></m:math></para>
                  <para id="para-00094"><m:math><m:mrow><m:mo stretchy="false">(</m:mo><m:mn>2</m:mn><m:mo>,</m:mo><m:mn>1</m:mn><m:mo stretchy="false">)</m:mo></m:mrow></m:math></para>
                  <para id="para-00095"><m:math><m:mrow><m:mo stretchy="false">(</m:mo><m:mn>4</m:mn><m:mo>,</m:mo><m:mi>−</m:mi><m:mn>2</m:mn><m:mo stretchy="false">)</m:mo></m:mrow></m:math></para>
                  <para id="para-00096"><m:math><m:mrow><m:mo stretchy="false">(</m:mo><m:mn>0</m:mn><m:mo>,</m:mo><m:mn>4</m:mn><m:mo stretchy="false">)</m:mo></m:mrow></m:math></para>
               </problem>
               <solution id="sol-00008">
                  <para id="para-00097">Correct! (4,−2)</para>
                  <para id="para-00098">Try again. Revisit activities 2.3.3 and 2.3.4.</para>
                  <para id="para-00099">The correct answer is (4,−2).</para>
                  <para id="para-00100">Check the solution in both equations.</para>
                  <para id="para-00101">\(\begin{array}{rcl}y&amp;=&amp;x−6 \\ -2&amp;=&amp;(4)−6 \\
                     -2&amp;=&amp;−2\checkmark \\ \end{array}\)</para>
                  <para id="para-00102">\(\begin{array}{rcl}y&amp;=&amp;−32x+4 \\ -2&amp;=&amp;−32(4)+4 \\
                     -2&amp;=&amp;−6+4 \\ -2&amp;=&amp;-2\checkmark \\ \end{array}\)</para>
                  <para id="para-00103">(4,−2) Makes both equations in the system true, therefore it is a solution.</para>
               </solution>
            </exercise>
            <exercise id="_401e6494-8f33-4e4d-b593-16e163d0cb2b" class="multiple-choice">
               <problem id="prob-00009">
                  <para id="para-00104"><m:math><m:mrow><m:mrow><m:mo stretchy="true" fence="true" form="prefix">{</m:mo><m:mtable><m:mtr><m:mtd columnalign="left"><m:mn>2</m:mn><m:mi>x</m:mi><m:mo>−</m:mo><m:mn>16</m:mn><m:mi>y</m:mi><m:mo>=</m:mo><m:mn>8</m:mn></m:mtd></m:mtr><m:mtr><m:mtd columnalign="left"><m:mo>−</m:mo><m:mi>x</m:mi><m:mo>−</m:mo><m:mn>8</m:mn><m:mi>y</m:mi><m:mo>=</m:mo><m:mo>−</m:mo><m:mn>4</m:mn></m:mtd></m:mtr></m:mtable><m:mo stretchy="true" fence="true" form="postfix"/></m:mrow></m:mrow></m:math></para>
                  <para id="para-00105">Multiple Choice:</para>
                  <para id="para-00106"><m:math><m:mrow><m:mo stretchy="false">(</m:mo><m:mn>12</m:mn><m:mo>,</m:mo><m:mn>1</m:mn><m:mo stretchy="false">)</m:mo></m:mrow></m:math></para>
                  <para id="para-00107"><m:math><m:mrow><m:mo stretchy="false">(</m:mo><m:mn>4</m:mn><m:mo>,</m:mo><m:mn>0</m:mn><m:mo stretchy="false">)</m:mo></m:mrow></m:math></para>
                  <para id="para-00108"><m:math><m:mrow><m:mo stretchy="false">(</m:mo><m:mi>−</m:mi><m:mn>4</m:mn><m:mo>,</m:mo><m:mn>1</m:mn><m:mo stretchy="false">)</m:mo></m:mrow></m:math></para>
                  <para id="para-00109"><m:math><m:mrow><m:mo stretchy="false">(</m:mo><m:mi>−</m:mi><m:mn>4</m:mn><m:mo>,</m:mo><m:mi>−</m:mi><m:mn>1</m:mn><m:mo stretchy="false">)</m:mo></m:mrow></m:math></para>
               </problem>
               <solution id="sol-00009">
                  <para id="para-00110">Correct! (4,0)</para>
                  <para id="para-00111">Try again. Revisit activities 2.3.3 and 2.3.4.</para>
                  <para id="para-00112">The correct answer is (4,0).</para>
                  <para id="para-00113">Check the solution in both equations.</para>
                  <para id="para-00114">\(\begin{array}{rcl} 2x−16y&amp;=&amp;8 \\ 2(4)−16(0)&amp;=&amp;8 \\
                     8-0&amp;=&amp;8 \\ 8&amp;=&amp;8\checkmark \\ \end{array}\)</para>
                  <para id="para-00115">\(\begin{array}{rcl} −x−8y&amp;=&amp;−4 \\ −4−8(0)&amp;=&amp;−4 \\
                     -4−0&amp;=&amp;−4 \\ -4&amp;=&amp;-4\checkmark \\ \end{array}\)</para>
                  <para id="para-00116">(4,0) Makes both equations in the system true, therefore it is a solution.</para>
               </solution>
            </exercise>
            <exercise id="_16baa37a-12b3-4828-97a4-45ccf7b841bd" class="multiple-choice">
               <problem id="prob-00010">
                  <para id="para-00117"><m:math><m:mrow><m:mrow><m:mo stretchy="true" fence="true" form="prefix">{</m:mo><m:mtable><m:mtr><m:mtd columnalign="left"><m:mi>y</m:mi><m:mo>=</m:mo><m:mo>−</m:mo><m:mfrac><m:mn>2</m:mn><m:mn>3</m:mn></m:mfrac><m:mi>x</m:mi><m:mo>+</m:mo><m:mn>6</m:mn></m:mtd></m:mtr><m:mtr><m:mtd columnalign="left"><m:mn>2</m:mn><m:mi>x</m:mi><m:mo>−</m:mo><m:mi>y</m:mi><m:mo>=</m:mo><m:mn>2</m:mn></m:mtd></m:mtr></m:mtable><m:mo stretchy="true" fence="true" form="postfix"/></m:mrow></m:mrow></m:math></para>
                  <para id="para-00118">Multiple Choice:</para>
                  <para id="para-00119"><m:math><m:mrow><m:mo stretchy="false">(</m:mo><m:mn>0</m:mn><m:mo>,</m:mo><m:mn>6</m:mn><m:mo stretchy="false">)</m:mo></m:mrow></m:math></para>
                  <para id="para-00120"><m:math><m:mrow><m:mo stretchy="false">(</m:mo><m:mi>−</m:mi><m:mn>2</m:mn><m:mo>,</m:mo><m:mn>0</m:mn><m:mo stretchy="false">)</m:mo></m:mrow></m:math></para>
                  <para id="para-00121"><m:math><m:mrow><m:mo stretchy="false">(</m:mo><m:mn>3</m:mn><m:mo>,</m:mo><m:mn>4</m:mn><m:mo stretchy="false">)</m:mo></m:mrow></m:math></para>
                  <para id="para-00122"><m:math><m:mrow><m:mo stretchy="false">(</m:mo><m:mn>6</m:mn><m:mo>,</m:mo><m:mn>2</m:mn><m:mo stretchy="false">)</m:mo></m:mrow></m:math></para>
               </problem>
               <solution id="sol-00010">
                  <para id="para-00123">Correct! (3,4)</para>
                  <para id="para-00124">Try again. Revisit activities 2.3.3 and 2.3.4.</para>
                  <para id="para-00125">The correct answer is (3, 4).</para>
                  <para id="para-00126">Check the solution in both equations.</para>
                  <para id="para-00127">\(\begin{array}{rcl}y&amp;=&amp;−\frac23x+6 \\ 4&amp;=&amp;−\frac23(3)+6 \\
                     4&amp;=&amp;−2+6 \\ 4&amp;=&amp;4\checkmark\\ \end{array}\)</para>
                  <para id="para-00128">\(\begin{array}{rcl} 2(3)−(4)&amp;=&amp;2 \\ 6−4&amp;=&amp;2 \\
                     2&amp;=&amp;2\checkmark \\ \end{array}\)</para>
                  <para id="para-00129">(3,4) Makes both equations in the system true, therefore it is a solution.</para>
               </solution>
            </exercise>
            <exercise id="_658cf1ee-cc3d-4df0-ba52-cd6e1eac9d07" class="multiple-choice">
               <problem id="prob-00011">
                  <para id="para-00130">Tyler and Han are trying to solve this system by substitution:</para>
                  <para id="para-00131"><m:math><m:mrow><m:mrow><m:mo stretchy="true" fence="true" form="prefix">{</m:mo><m:mtable><m:mtr><m:mtd columnalign="left"><m:mi>x</m:mi><m:mo>+</m:mo><m:mn>3</m:mn><m:mi>y</m:mi><m:mo>=</m:mo><m:mo>−</m:mo><m:mn>5</m:mn></m:mtd></m:mtr><m:mtr><m:mtd columnalign="left"><m:mn>9</m:mn><m:mi>x</m:mi><m:mo>+</m:mo><m:mn>3</m:mn><m:mi>y</m:mi><m:mo>=</m:mo><m:mn>3</m:mn></m:mtd></m:mtr></m:mtable><m:mo stretchy="true" fence="true" form="postfix"/></m:mrow></m:mrow></m:math></para>
                  <para id="para-00132">Tyler's first step is to isolate x in the first equation to get \(x = -5 -
                     3y.\)</para>
                  <para id="para-00133">Han's first step is to isolate 3y in the first equation to get \(3y = -5 -
                     x.\)</para>
                  <para id="para-00134">Solve using both methods to show that both first steps can be used to solve
                     the system and will yield the same solution.</para>
                  <para id="para-00135">What is the solution to the system?</para>
                  <para id="para-00136">Multiple Choice:</para>
                  <para id="para-00137"><m:math><m:mrow><m:mo stretchy="false">(</m:mo><m:mn>1</m:mn><m:mo>,</m:mo><m:mo>−</m:mo><m:mn>2</m:mn><m:mo stretchy="false">)</m:mo></m:mrow></m:math></para>
                  <para id="para-00138"><m:math><m:mrow><m:mo stretchy="false">(</m:mo><m:mn>0</m:mn><m:mo>,</m:mo><m:mn>1</m:mn><m:mo stretchy="false">)</m:mo></m:mrow></m:math></para>
                  <para id="para-00139"><m:math><m:mrow><m:mo stretchy="false">(</m:mo><m:mn>4</m:mn><m:mo>,</m:mo><m:mo>−</m:mo><m:mn>3</m:mn><m:mo stretchy="false">)</m:mo></m:mrow></m:math></para>
                  <para id="para-00140"><m:math><m:mrow><m:mo stretchy="false">(</m:mo><m:mo>−</m:mo><m:mn>5</m:mn><m:mo>,</m:mo><m:mn>0</m:mn><m:mo stretchy="false">)</m:mo></m:mrow></m:math></para>
               </problem>
               <solution id="sol-00011">
                  <para id="para-00141">Correct! (1,-2)</para>
                  <para id="para-00142">Try again. Revisit activity 2.3.3.</para>
                  <para id="para-00143">The correct answer is (1,-2).</para>
                  <para id="para-00144">Check the solution in both equations.</para>
                  <para id="para-00145">\(\begin{array}{rcl} x+3y&amp;=&amp;−5 \\ 1+3(-2)&amp;=&amp;−5 \\
                     1-6&amp;=&amp;−5 \\ -5&amp;=&amp;-5\checkmark \\ \end{array}\)</para>
                  <para id="para-00146">\(\begin{array}{rcl} 9x+3y&amp;=&amp;3 \\ 9(1)+3(-2)&amp;=&amp;3 \\
                     9-6&amp;=&amp;3 \\ 3&amp;=&amp;3\checkmark \\ \end{array}\)</para>
                  <para id="para-00147">(1,-2) Makes both equations in the system true, therefore it is a solution.</para>
               </solution>
            </exercise>
      </section>
   </content>
